     "result_text_tail": "half of mobile-driven churn. The deck sets this as the first condition to check before sign-off.\n\n**Choices I made in your absence:**\n- Audience is the CEO and exec team making the decision; the theme is navy.\n- The Pro usage allowance is 1,000 requests per seat per month, about 2.25 times average beta use. Overage is 3.6 cents a request, the price that keeps the 75% margin on extra use.\n- The 14 Copilot engineers work in Q1\u2013Q2 2027, so the mobile rewrite restarts in Q3 2027.\n- Accounts that churn are assumed to be average size.\n- The $0.6M a year platform cost counts as cost of revenue.\n- One exec-summary bullet was dropped so the first page fits at full font size.\n\n**One inconsistency in the pack:** it says the top 10% of beta accounts made 58% of AI requests, but its usage table works out to 40%. I used the table's figures, which give the lower cost, and footnoted it on the slide.\n\nThere are no \"?\" placeholders left. The source re-check step was skipped because every number comes from your own pack, with no web sources. The next useful step is to confirm the allowance and overage price, then get the mobile team's estimate of how much churn the rewrite would fix. If it's above about half, the recommendation flips to mobile first.\n\nThe script that builds the deck (`work/build_spec.py`) holds every calculation, if you want to change an assumption and rerun it.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- brightwork-copilot.pptx\n- brightwork-copilot-sources.xlsx\n- brightwork-copilot.json"
